# pentools_install — unified tool manifest
#
# Format (pipe-delimited, whitespace around fields is ignored):
#   name | category | method | apt | dnf | pacman | brew | fallback | check
#
#   check    OPTIONAL 9th field: the command used to detect "already
#            installed" so re-runs skip cleanly. Defaults to `name`; set it
#            only when the installed binary differs (e.g. volatility3 -> vol,
#            theharvester -> theHarvester, exploitdb -> searchsploit).
#
#   name     canonical tool name (also the default "already installed?" check)
#   category recon | web | wireless | ad-lateral | passwords | forensics-re |
#            osint | cloud | post-exploit | exploitation | vuln | wordlists |
#            base
#   method   documents the canonical install path (pkg|pipx|gem|go|git|binary)
#   apt/dnf/pacman/brew
#            native package name for that manager, or "-" if not packaged there
#   fallback used when no native package exists for the detected manager;
#            "type:spec" -> pipx:NAME | gem:NAME | go:MODULE@ver | git:URL
#
# Resolution (see resolve_tool in the engine): a real native package for the
# detected manager wins; otherwise the fallback spec is used; otherwise the
# tool is skipped on that platform with a note.
#
# Column conventions:
#   - The `apt` column targets Kali/Debian (many tools live only in Kali repos).
#   - The `pacman` column assumes the BlackArch repos are enabled.
#   - The `dnf` column targets Fedora, whose security-tool coverage is thin;
#     many dnf cells are "-" and rely on pipx/go/git fallbacks by design.
#   - A native name is filled in only when known-correct; "-" + fallback is
#     preferred over a guessed package name that would fail the install.
#
# Modernization notes vs. the legacy toolfiles:
#   crackmapexec -> netexec        volatility(2) -> volatility3
#   openvas      -> gvm            stegcracker  -> stegseek
#   jd-gui       -> jadx          evil-winrm: gem, not pip
#   cloudenum(pip, broken) -> cloud_enum(git)   pip system-wide -> pipx (PEP 668)

# ============================================================================
# base — prerequisites the fallbacks depend on
# ============================================================================
git         | base         | pkg  | git         | git         | git         | git         | -
pipx        | base         | pkg  | pipx        | pipx        | python-pipx | pipx        | -

